Snorkel
=======

Snorkel is a modified version of devourer
(https://github.com/OpenIPC/devourer), the OpenIPC project's userspace
Realtek Wi-Fi driver. It is distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2, the same terms as devourer; see LICENSE.

Forked from devourer at commit 1134df9 (October 2026).
Snorkel changes: Copyright (C) 2026 Christopher Arquiza.

All copyright and license notices in devourer's files, including Realtek's
and the BSD-licensed MediaTek and vendor files, are unchanged. The git
history records every change in detail; this file summarises them, as
section 2(a) of the GPL asks.


Files changed from devourer (October 2026)
------------------------------------------

Station client and core

  tests/sta_client.cpp
      Runs on macOS: the host side is a fake-Ethernet pair (feth), read with
      BPF and written with NDRV, instead of a Linux TAP device. Adds 802.11n
      association, Block Ack with receive reordering, A-MSDU unpacking, a
      base rate for management frames, response-rate and DIG settings, and
      a periodic link log.
  tests/sta_client_selftest.inc, tests/station_sm_selftest.cpp
      Tests for the above.
  src/sta/Dot11.h
      HT Capabilities and WMM elements; ADDBA request/response frames.
  src/sta/StationSm.h
      HT association and Block Ack agreements; a fix for a clock wrap that
      reported false beacon loss.

Driver

  src/IRtlRadio.h, src/jaguar2/RtlJaguar2Device.{h,cpp}
      SetResponseRates: set the rates the chip answers with (RRSR).
  src/jaguar2/HalJaguar2.cpp
      Sets the 5 GHz synthesizer band bits on every 5 GHz tune (a 2.4 to
      5 GHz retune left the chip deaf); a configurable DIG ceiling.
  src/DeviceConfig.h, examples/common/env_config.cpp
      The DIG ceiling setting (DEVOURER_IGI_MAX).

Build, tests and documentation

  CMakeLists.txt
      Builds the station client on macOS; adds the reorder test.
  .github/workflows/
      Adds a macOS station CI job; removes upstream's review-bot gate.
  README.md
      Replaced with Snorkel's README. devourer's README is DEVOURER.md,
      unchanged except for one link to the macOS guide.
  CLAUDE.md, src/sta/CLAUDE.md, docs/station-client.md, .gitignore
      Notes for the changes above.


